# =============================================================================
# Build and run outputs of the Python interface.
#
# obj/, lib/ and __pycache__/ are produced by `make` and by the interpreter and
# are removed by `make clean`; the scheduler writes gmg_py_<jobid>.out wherever
# the job was submitted from.
#
# Job scripts (*.slurm) and the alternative input PARA_INPUT_np2.inp stay local:
# they are site- and run-specific, so they are ignored rather than tracked.
# Note that ignoring them only works while they are untracked -- a path already
# in the index is unaffected by these rules and has to be dropped with
# `git rm --cached` first.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#   run/PARA_INPUT.inp
#                   the reference problem definition, not build output.
#   environment.yml, setup_env.sh
#                   part of the deliverable.
#
# The repository root .gitignore already covers *.o, *.so and obj/; the entries
# below repeat the ones that matter here so this directory is self-describing.
# =============================================================================
obj/
lib/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scheduler output of the job scripts
gmg_py_*.out

# Job scripts. The leading * is required: a bare `.slurm` matches only a file
# named exactly that, not every name ending in .slurm.
*.slurm

PARA_INPUT_np2.inp
